{"Backup codes consumption leaves null entries in codes array by setting backupCodes[index] = null, which will cause UI breakage when formatBackupCode receives null": 0.5627273321151733, "Missing imports for React/Hooks in TwoFactor component - useState and useFormContext are used but not imported, causing compile/runtime errors": 0.05021804943680763, "Disable-2FA API path with backup code does not actually disable 2FA - it validates the backup code but does not update the user record to clear backupCodes or twoFactorEnabled": 0.04692923650145531, "Missing encryption key (CALENDSO_ENCRYPTION_KEY) causes server error without fallback handling, leading to server instability in misconfigured environments": 0.21811319887638092, "No end-to-end Playwright test covers signing in using a backup code after 2FA is required": 0.44012048840522766, "AES algorithm name 'aes256' in crypto module may be invalid - Node.js expects named cipher like 'aes-256-cbc' or 'aes-256-ctr'": 0.018262773752212524, "EnableTwoFactorModal.tsx renders backupCodes array without filtering out nulls, causing formatBackupCode to fail or display 'null'": 0.13425248861312866, "DisableTwoFactorModal calls TwoFactorAuthAPI.disable with only two arguments (password, totpCode) but API expects three parameters including backupCode": 0.0039610168896615505, "Backup codes are exposed in API response during TOTP setup - potential leakage beyond onboarding step": 0.2138388603925705, "Existing users with 2FA enabled but no backup codes will have null backupCodes, but code paths assume an encrypted string when decrypting": 0.6868523955345154, "Potential duplication of UI logic across BackupCode.tsx, EnableTwoFactorModal backup codes screen, and login Lost Access backup codes": 0.00732149975374341, "No explicit UI path to reset or display fresh state after disabling 2FA when backupCodes are cleared to null": 0.012443077750504017, "New i18n keys for backup codes added to English locale but may need analogous updates in